      "reason": "ADDED BY RECONCILIATION (metadata-writer): named in BrandResearch''s Namespaces list but absent from SourceAudit''s 27-entry outOfScopeFamilies list. WooCommerce 11.0.1 ships a GraphQL endpoint behind the `dual_code_graphql_api` feature flag and PHP 8.1+ (src/Api/Infrastructure/Main.php FEATURE_SLUG; src/Api/Infrastructure/GraphQLControllerBase.php register() splits the configured endpoint URL `wc/v4/graphql` into [''wc/v4'',''/graphql'']). Not on a stock install (0 live routes) and it MUST NOT change APIParadigm — REST remains correct at these pins — but it is a NON-REST addressing scheme with its own Principal/PrincipalResolver auth model (permission_callback => __return_true, auth handled per-query/mutation) and its endpoint PATH is a site option rather than a fixed route, so it is not even enumerable as a stable path. Out of scope for 1.0.0; recorded because a future Woo release flipping the flag would introduce a second paradigm."
    },
    {
      "family": "View Config",
      "namespace": "wp/v2",
      "kind": "route-level-informational",
      "familiesInUniverse": 1,
      "routesInUniverse": 1,
      "registrationEvidence": "bootstrap-verified",
      "reason": "DEMOTED OUT OF THE RECORD CATALOG BY PROBEAMEND (was declared as the ViewConfig IO). The route IS registered (wp-includes/rest-api.php:437 instantiates WP_REST_View_Config_Controller and calls register_routes()), but WP_REST_View_Config_Controller::register_routes() registers exactly ONE route with exactly ONE READABLE endpoint whose args are kind (required:true) and name (required:true) and NOTHING else — no page/per_page/context, no item route, no collection params (class-wp-rest-view-config-controller.php:35-60). It is a PARAMETERISED SINGLETON LOOKUP, not a listable collection: get_items() returns ONE associative document {kind,name,version,default_view,default_layouts,view_list,form} (lines 147-165), every property of get_item_schema() is readonly:true (lines 249-389), and the payload is computed by wp_get_entity_view_config($kind,$name) from the registered post types/taxonomies plus the get_entity_view_config_{$kind}_{$name} filter — a derived UI configuration document, NOT a stored site record. There is also NO way to enumerate the (kind,name) universe from this route, so it has no syncable record set at all. This is the same class as the already-informational BlockPatternCategory / BlockPatternPattern (\"registered at runtime; no durable stored record\") and BlockRenderer (\"the {name} is a block type, not a record\"): it belongs in InformationalRoutes. Consequently the prior declaration''s listPath/responseShape=''array''/SupportsPagination=true/PaginationType=PageNumber/SyncStrategy=''SnapshotReplace'' were all unsupportable, and PK was already unset (one of the 5 deliberately PK-unset objects). Removing it drops the declared catalog from 79 to 78 record types, 1059 to 1052 fields and 223 to 222 paths."
    }
  ],
  "OutOfScopeObjectFamiliesNote": "DEVIATION D3 — this is SourceAudit''s RECONCILED list (sources.json outOfScopeFamilies, 27 entries, carried VERBATIM with every reason, familiesInUniverse, routesInUniverse and registrationEvidence value preserved), NOT the plan''s shorter literal. Six entries are honestly marked `code-present-registration-unverified` and that qualifier is load-bearing: it means the controllers declare routes + a namespace but the code instantiating them lies outside the acquired file set. A 28th entry (wc/v4/graphql) was ADDED by reconciliation against BrandResearch''s Namespaces list. Total 28. Third-party plugin entries (mp/v1, pmpro/v1, gf/v2, ldlms/v2, tribe/events/v1) are the operator''s KNOWING 1.0.0 scope decision; the first-party entries came from independent study and would otherwise be invisible.",
  "DeclaredCapabilityLimits": [
    {
      "id": "users-no-incremental",
      "scope": "wp/v2/users",
      "reason": "wp/v2/users exposes NO date filter and NO modified timestamp. get_collection_params() yields exactly: context, page, per_page, search, search_columns, exclude, include, offset, order, orderby, slug, roles, capabilities, who, has_published_posts — and the string ''modified'' does not occur anywhere in class-wp-rest-users-controller.php (0 occurrences, independently reproduced). The record schema DOES carry `registered_date`, and `orderby` DOES accept `registered_date` (mapped to WP_User_Query orderby `registered` at class-wp-rest-users-controller.php:310).",
      "capabilityPrecise": "FULL-SCAN, or at most an INSERT-ONLY HIGH-WATER scan ordered by registered_date. This narrow capability is PROVEN, not assumed — but UPDATES to existing users are INVISIBLE to any delta strategy, because no modified timestamp exists to compare against.",
      "consequence": "No IncrementalWatermarkField may be emitted on users. No delta test cell may simulate one. The insert-only high-water capability may be declared EXACTLY as stated and must never be rounded up to \"incremental supported\".",
      "additionalGate": "The insert-only high-water path is ITSELF capability-gated: class-wp-rest-users-controller.php:228 rejects orderby=registered_date (and orderby=email) unless the caller has `list_users`. An under-privileged credential therefore loses even this narrow capability and degrades to unordered full-scan.",
      "evidence": "packages/Integration/connectors-registry/wordpress/sources/wp-7.1/wp-includes/rest-api/endpoints/class-wp-rest-users-controller.php:228,310,1101-1102,1490"
    },
    {
      "id": "woo-customers-no-incremental",
      "scope": "wc/v3/customers",
      "reason": "DEVIATION D2 — NOT in the script''s literal limit list. wc/v3/customers does NOT extend WC_REST_CRUD_Controller. The chain is WC_REST_Customers_Controller -> WC_REST_Customers_V2_Controller -> WC_REST_Customers_V1_Controller -> WC_REST_Controller -> WP_REST_Controller (independently reproduced from the class declarations), so it inherits NONE of the date params defined on WC_REST_CRUD_Controller: no `after`, no `before`, no `modified_after`, no `dates_are_gmt` (0 occurrences of any of them across all three customers controller files; contrast class-wc-rest-crud-controller.php:308,331,334,608,620 where they are all defined).",
      "capabilityPrecise": "FULL-SCAN, or an INSERT-ONLY HIGH-WATER scan via orderby=registered_date — EXACTLY the same narrow capability as wp/v2/users, not a weaker one and not a full watermark. Proven: the orderby enum [id, include, name, registered_date] at class-wc-rest-customers-v1-controller.php:1027, mapped to WP_User_Query orderby `registered` at :358.",
      "consequence": "UPDATES INVISIBLE. No watermark field on customers, and no simulated customers delta cell. This entry exists because the context notes'' phrasing (\"WooCommerce orders/products support modified_after\") would lead straight to emitting a watermark on customers that does not exist.",
      "evidence": "packages/Integration/connectors-registry/wordpress/sources/woocommerce-11.0.1/includes/rest-api/Controllers/Version1/class-wc-rest-customers-v1-controller.php:358,1027 ; Version{1,2,3}/class-wc-rest-customers*.php:19,21,25 (chain) ; Version3/class-wc-rest-crud-controller.php:608,620 (contrast)"
    },
    {
      "id": "no-deleted-records-feed",
      "scope": "wp/v2 (all) + wc/v3 (all)",
      "reason": "There is NO deleted-records feed anywhere in wp/v2 or wc/v3. `status=trash` covers SOFT deletes for post types ONLY; a hard delete (DELETE ?force=true) vanishes leaving NO tombstone of any kind.",
      "consequence": "Deletion reconciliation requires a periodic KEY SWEEP (compare the full remote ID set against the local set). The connector must DECLARE the key sweep rather than pretend to DETECT deletions. It must not claim delete detection.",
      "evidence": "brand.json CapabilityTable.incremental.deletes ; brand.json WriteCapability.bindingNote (BINDING under floor rule capability-dishonest)"
    },
    {
      "id": "capability-gated-field-visibility",
      "scope": "wp/v2 + wc/v3 — per-field, per-credential",
      "reason": "Many fields are exposed only for context=edit PLUS the corresponding capability (e.g. a user''s email and registered_date). OPTIONS <route> returns a real JSON Schema, but the schema a caller receives is filtered by that caller''s capabilities.",
      "consequence": "An under-privileged credential SILENTLY returns a THINNER schema than the docs describe. Field ABSENCE at runtime therefore proves NOTHING about the vendor, and NO discovery result may deactivate a declared field. The derived catalog is the MAXIMUM a fully-privileged credential sees, not a per-connection guarantee.",
      "evidence": "brand.json CapabilityTable.authoritativeEnumeration.fieldLevel ; sources.json Gaps[\"Field-level completeness under a real credential\"] ; class-wp-rest-users-controller.php:228 (orderby gated on list_users)"
    },
    {
      "id": "offset-pagination-drift",
      "scope": "wp/v2 + wc/v3 — every paginated collection",
      "reason": "`page`/`per_page` is OFFSET-based page numbering, not keyset/cursor. Concurrent writes shift rows across page boundaries during a deep scan, so records can be skipped or duplicated.",
      "consequence": "Completeness of a deep full-scan is BEST-EFFORT. The mitigation is a stable sort (orderby=id&order=asc), which reduces but does not eliminate drift. Exactness must never be claimed.",
      "evidence": "packages/Integration/connectors-registry/wordpress/sources/wp-7.1/wp-includes/rest-api/endpoints/class-wp-rest-controller.php:352-357 (per_page default 10, minimum 1, maximum 100)"
    },
    {
      "id": "dual-namespace-credentials",
      "scope": "connection-level (wp/v2 vs wc/v3)",
      "reason": "One connection may need TWO credential shapes: an Application Password for wp/v2, and optionally a WooCommerce consumer key/secret for wc/v3. A Woo-only key pair CANNOT read wp/v2 at all — WC_REST_Authentication::is_request_to_rest_api() matches only URIs whose path after the REST prefix begins `wc/` or `wc-`.",
      "consequence": "A partially-provisioned credential yields a PARTIAL object set. That must surface as an EXPLICIT capability warning, never as an empty-but-green sync. Additionally, Application Passwords are unavailable over plain HTTP outside a local environment (wp-includes/user.php:5156 `return is_ssl() || ''local'' === wp_get_environment_type();`), which is why the credential schema expresses the two pairs as `anyOf` rather than both hard-required.",
      "evidence": "identity.json CredentialTypeResolution.AsymmetryWarningForCodeBuilder ; woocommerce-11.0.1/includes/class-wc-rest-authentication.php:69-83 ; wp-7.1/wp-includes/user.php:5156"
    },
    {
      "id": "setting-write-unavailable-no-pk",
      "scope": "wp/v2/settings (IO: Setting)",
      "fact": "The vendor DOES support writing site settings — POST /wp/v2/settings with a flat body, no {id} segment. But wp/v2/settings is a SINGLETON: one row, addressed with no identifier at all, so the object has no primary key (PK deliberately unset at extraction — identity genuinely absent).",
      "consequence": "MJ save paths identify a row by primary key, so a writable object with no PK cannot be saved (the lint-writable-pk gate rejects it, and on PostgreSQL the write could not execute). This connector therefore declares the write surface UNAVAILABLE for Setting rather than fabricating an identity the vendor does not expose. Reads are unaffected.",
      "classification": "FRAMEWORK EXPRESSIVENESS GAP, not a vendor limitation — MJ cannot currently express a writable singleton. If that is added, restore SupportsWrite/SupportsUpdate plus UpdateAPIPath=/wp/v2/settings, UpdateMethod=POST, UpdateBodyShape=flat, UpdateIDLocation=n/a."
    }
  ],
  "DeclaredCapabilityLimitsNote": "Six machine-readable entries, each an honest limitation that a lazy build would paper over with a fake test cell. `woo-customers-no-incremental` is DEVIATION D2 — it is not in the plan''s literal list and was added on SourceAudit/BrandResearch evidence. Each entry carries scope + reason + consequence, and the two insert-only families carry `capabilityPrecise` so the narrow proven capability is not rounded up.",
  "AsyncOperationModel": "none",
  "AsyncOperationModelNote": "FULLY SYNCHRONOUS. No route in wp/v2, wc/v3 or /batch/v1 returns a job id, a 202-plus-poll handle, or an export-file handle — every request returns the final representation. WordPress does have background infrastructure (WP-Cron; Woo bundles Action Scheduler) but neither is exposed as a REST job API in the in-scope surface, so there is nothing to poll. Consequence: large extractions are bounded by per_page <= 100 and by request-time limits on the TENANT''S OWN host, not by a job queue — throughput is a function of the customer''s hosting, which the connector cannot know in advance.",
  "RelationshipModel": {
    "kinds": [
      "path-nesting",
      "scalar-fk-fields",
      "association-arrays"
    ],
    "note": "ALL THREE, MIXED — the connector cannot pick one strategy.",
    "pathNesting": "wp/v2/posts/<id>/revisions, wp/v2/posts/<id>/autosaves, wp/v2/templates/<id>/revisions, wp/v2/global-styles/<id>/revisions, wp/v2/users/<id>/application-passwords, wp/v2/menu-items, wc/v3/orders/<id>/notes, wc/v3/orders/<id>/refunds, wc/v3/products/<id>/variations, wc/v3/products/attributes/<id>/terms, wc/v3/shipping/zones/<id>/locations, wc/v3/shipping/zones/<id>/methods, wc/v3/customers/<id>/downloads.",
    "foreignKeyFields": "Scalar FK properties on the record: post.author, post.featured_media, post.parent, comment.post, comment.parent, media.post, order.customer_id, product_variation.parent_id, review.product_id, refund.parent_id.",
    "associationArrays": "Array-of-id or array-of-object properties: post.categories[], post.tags[], product.categories[], product.tags[], product.images[], product.attributes[], order.line_items[], order.tax_lines[], order.shipping_lines[], order.fee_lines[], order.coupon_lines[], order.meta_data[].",
    "fanOutWarning": "Nested COLLECTIONS require an N+1 fan-out from the parent''s id — there is no top-level listing for order notes, and while `refunds` and `variations` DO exist as top-level wc/v3 routes (an undocumented convenience), order notes have none. Registered `meta` is a nested object whose keys are per-site (only meta registered with show_in_rest appears), which is a further per-site field-universe source distinct from the per-site OBJECT universe."
  },
  "FilterSearchModel": {
    "note": "There is NO generic filter DSL (no OData-style $filter, no arbitrary field predicates) — only the enumerated per-route args. An unrecognised arg is silently ignored rather than rejected, so a connector must never infer support from a 200 response; it must read the arg list from OPTIONS.",
    "core": "`search` (free text) on every collection, plus `search_columns` to restrict which columns are searched, plus per-collection filters: status, author, author_exclude, categories, categories_exclude, tags, tags_exclude, slug, sticky, ignore_sticky, format, tax_relation, parent, parent_exclude, include, exclude, offset, order, orderby. WP 7.1 additionally exposes a `search_semantics` arg on wp/v2/posts (observed via OPTIONS on the reference instance) — a new semantic-search hook worth noting as a 7.1-era addition.",
    "woo": "`search`, plus per-resource: status, type, sku, category, tag, attribute, attribute_term, on_sale, min_price, max_price, stock_status, featured, customer, product, created_via, reviewer, reviewer_email, role, email, code."
  },
  "APIParadigm": "REST",
  "APIParadigmNote": "REST is correct and dominant at the pinned versions. Two qualifications: (a) the REST surface is SELF-DESCRIBING (route index + per-route JSON Schema via OPTIONS), which is what makes public discovery authoritative for this vendor; (b) WooCommerce 11.0.1 SHIPS a GraphQL endpoint (wc/v4/graphql) behind the `dual_code_graphql_api` feature flag and PHP 8.1+, so the Woo paradigm is trending Hybrid even though a stock install is REST-only. WordPress also retains an XML-RPC endpoint (/xmlrpc.php) outside the REST surface — legacy, out of scope, and often disabled by hosts.",
  "MetadataWriterDeviations": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "slot": "Configuration.DiscoveryAuthoritativeness.objectLevel",
      "see": "DiscoveryAuthoritativeness.objectLevelRejectedValue / .objectLevelCaveats"
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "slot": "Configuration.DeclaredCapabilityLimits[woo-customers-no-incremental]",
      "see": "DeclaredCapabilityLimits — sixth entry, added"
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "slot": "Configuration.OutOfScopeObjectFamilies",
      "see": "OutOfScopeObjectFamiliesNote — reconciled 27 + 1 added"
    }
  ],
  "MetadataWriterDeviationsNote": "Recorded, never silent. BrandResearch''s findings are BINDING (v2 P5) and reality outranks the frozen contract, so where a prior phase''s evidence contradicted a literal in the MetadataWrite script, the evidence won. Full evidence for each: journal/deviations.json.",
  "KnownGaps": [
    {
      "area": "wp/v2 global styles enumeration",
      "reason": "core registers NO collection route for global-styles (only /wp/v2/global-styles/{id} plus /revisions), so the record ids cannot be listed from the API; a connector must reach them via the parent template/theme context. Declared coverable per the operator scope, but not independently enumerable.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "wc/v3 products/custom-fields/names",
      "reason": "registered and listable, but the controller declares NO record schema (the response is a bare string list). Recorded as informational by the zero-schema guard rather than shipped as a 0-field object.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "wc/v3 order fulfillments field model",
      "reason": "OrderFulfillment yielded only 3 statically derivable properties: the controller declares its shape in per-endpoint get_schema_for_*() methods that reference a base schema defined outside the parsed class chain (a trait). The family is real and coverable; its field model is thin and must be completed at extraction from the docs/handbook or a live OPTIONS call.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "Per-site object universe",
      "reason": "no pinned source can enumerate a per-site universe: plugin namespaces and site-registered custom post types/taxonomies are unknowable ahead of a connection. The declared catalog is the stock-install FLOOR; the remainder is reachable only by runtime route-index discovery, which is UNVERIFIED on this credential-free run.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "Rate limits",
      "reason": "neither wp/v2 nor wc/v3 documents any rate limit (core imposes none; real limits are host/CDN-imposed). No number can be recorded honestly — only the obligation to honour 429 + Retry-After. The one ecosystem API with documented RateLimit-* headers is the out-of-scope Store API.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "Registration evidence for 6 first-party namespaces",
      "reason": "wccom-site/v3, woocommerce-email-editor/v1, wc-admin-email, wc/pos/v1/catalog, wc-push-notifications and jetpack/v4 have controllers that declare routes + a namespace, but the code that instantiates them lives outside the acquired file set (service-container definitions / plugin bootstrap). They are in the universe as code-present-registration-unverified; BrandResearch observed all but wc-push-notifications on a live stock index.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "Field-level completeness under a real credential",
      "reason": "field visibility is capability-gated (context=edit + capability), so the derived schema is the MAXIMUM a fully privileged credential sees. An under-privileged credential returns a thinner schema; nothing in this phase can measure that without a credential.",
      "source": "SourceAudit"
    },
    {
      "area": "Webhook signature algorithm + header",
      "reason": "NULL, not guessed. Woo''s webhook delivery/signing code (includes/class-wc-webhook.php) is not in the acquired pinned file set — the local Woo 11.0.1 extraction covers includes/rest-api, includes/admin and includes/wccom-site only. See Configuration.WebhooksSignatureGap.",
      "source": "MetadataWriter"
    },
    {
      "area": "Woo ETag generator call site",
      "reason": "get_data_for_etag() is OVERRIDDEN in the Woo products v2 controller but the base class that CALLS it is outside the acquired file set, so the mechanism cannot be characterised beyond \"not a client-supplied concurrency token\". ConcurrencyControl stays `none`. See Configuration.ConcurrencyControlNote.",
      "source": "MetadataWriter"
    },
    {
      "area": "BatchMaxRequestCount / BatchRequestWaitTime",
      "reason": "Both NULL — the accurate answer, not a gap in research. WordPress is self-hosted, so there is no vendor-stated per-app rate limit for wp/v2 or wc/v3; throttling is host-imposed and per-tenant. The per-request batch SIZES (core 25, Woo 100) are recorded under Configuration.BatchCapability, where they belong — they are payload caps, not rate limits, and conflating them into these two columns would misreport a rate limit that does not exist.",
      "source": "MetadataWriter"
    },
    {
      "area": "Runtime route-index discovery",
      "reason": "The per-site remainder is reachable only by runtime route-index discovery, which is UNVERIFIED on this credential-free [B]-posture run. No live connection was made.",
      "source": "MetadataWriter"
    }
  ]
